      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T21:01:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am curious how you decided the speeds in which to enable the speed features. Did you try to maintain evenly-spaced gaps between the speeds?\n\n(You don\u0027t need to add your reply to the commit message.)",
      "revId": "5ff60561be1f117002919e78f972a6319f98e54e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab1b23f4_bca1f6be",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T23:09:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I basically tried to keep an acceptable level of intraBC overhead and efficiency tradeoffs for each speed level.\n\nEach speed feature reduces the search space further and further, and proportionally impacts efficiency more and more.\n\nprune_intrabc_candidate_block_hash gives us the best \"bang for our buck\", while intrabc_search_level gives us the least.",
      "parentUuid": "cac1b3d6_76d80461",
      "revId": "5ff60561be1f117002919e78f972a6319f98e54e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de627c22_9c8557b2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T21:01:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[This comment is a discussion, not a request for change.] These numbers look great. Thanks!\n\nBut the PSNR increase doesn\u0027t seem to make sense. The three new speed features all prune searches. If we are pruning searhces, the best result should not be better than the best result of full searches. Can you explain this? Is it because we are NOT optimizing for PSNR?",
      "revId": "5ff60561be1f117002919e78f972a6319f98e54e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f40f3d97_247f1fe6",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T21:01:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you please summarize the improvements in the CHANGELOG? The intended audience is the end users, so no need to mention the new speed features, which are implementation details.",
      "revId": "5ff60561be1f117002919e78f972a6319f98e54e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "217307ce_bc844580",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T23:09:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe what\u0027s happening is that intraBC blocks tend to be very cheap to encode, but are overall slightly less quality compared to a regular intra encoded block. This means the RDO process will prefer picking the intraBC block, as the rdcost will be overall lower (i.e. the much smaller rate will make up for the slightly larger distortion).\n\nIf you prune out intraBC candidates, the RDO process will pick regular intra block candidates more often, so you\u0027ll end up with slightly less distorted but larger files. If you notice, the after encoded image is 4 kB bigger than the before.\n\nI also discovered the \"No intraBC\" images also had palette mode disabled by mistake. I\u0027ve amended the tables with files encoded with palette mode. This confirms the observation mentioned above.",
      "parentUuid": "de627c22_9c8557b2",
      "revId": "5ff60561be1f117002919e78f972a6319f98e54e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
